  "id": "COMPOUND:15278 - PROTEIN:5764",
  "verbalization": "Abiesadine E is shown to interact with Tyrosine--tRNA ligase, mitochondrial, which is a key enzyme in mitochondrial protein synthesis. This enzyme is targeted by multiple compounds, including (2s)-2-[(n-Benzoylphenylalanyl)amino]-3-phenylpropyl acetate and (1S,2S,4R,6R,8S,9R,10R,13R,14R,17S)-8,17-dihydroxy-2,8,10,13,18,18-hexamethyl-6-(2-methylprop-1-enyl)-5-oxapentacyclo[11.8.0.02,10.04,9.014,19]henicos-19-en-12-one, both of which are known to target T-24. The evidence suggests that Abiesadine E may exert its effects through a mechanism involving the inhibition of Tyrosine--tRNA ligase, mitochondrial, thereby potentially affecting mitochondrial protein synthesis in T-24 cells. The consistent targeting of this enzyme by multiple compounds and its association with T-24 indicates a plausible mechanism of action, though further validation with in vitro and in vivo studies is needed to confirm the specific role of Abiesadine E in T-24 cell function.",
